summary: The content changes a stamp cannot see.

!! Content a stamp cannot see

A side's content counts as changed when its size, mtime, kind or link target did
([[Change detection in sync]]). A rewrite of the same size within the same second is
missed, as by the watcher. A content hash in the stamp would see it, at the cost of
hashing every changed file on both sides — which the planner, comparing bytes only
when a stamp moved, avoids today.

The matching of records without a position, or moved before their first sync, is
settled: [[Why records are matched only by position]].
